 "meaning": "which typed canonical assertions (class/activity:attribute path, Java regex, whole match) an independent oracle property judges against native evidence, which are Journal's own provenance or caption siblings of a judged id, and which the caller declares; every other path is unjudged and inventoried by CrossCliAccountingTest. A basis string is text the writer wrote and is never judged: it stays unjudged on purpose. The property names are the oracle's (OcsfOracle.MANDATORY_SOURCE or the assembly oracle); this table is the reviewer's reading of OcsfOracle's value checks, pinned by hash so a change is a reviewable event. basis_text names the writer's free-text basis and derivation members: inventoried in their own bucket, never judged and never counted as judged. Keys are <profile>|<class>/<activity>:<path>, the profile being the source profile of the event's native artifact (assembly for an event consolidated from several), so a judgement can be stated for one source profile and left unjudged for another",
 "journal_origin": [
